  "question": {
    "text": "In a metal deficient oxide sample, $\\mathbf{M}_{\\mathbf{x}} \\mathbf{Y}_2 \\mathbf{O}_4$ ( $\\mathbf{M}$ and $\\mathbf{Y}$ are metals), $\\mathbf{M}$ is present in both +2 and +3 oxidation states and $\\mathbf{Y}$ is in +3 oxidation state. If the fraction of $\\mathbf{M}^{2+}$ ions present in $\\mathbf{M}$ is $\\frac{1}{3}$, the value of $\\mathbf{X}$ is ________."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "0.25",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.33",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.67",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "0.75",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Average oxidation state of $\\mathrm{M}=\\frac{1}{3} \\times 2+\\frac{2}{3} \\times 3=+\\frac{8}{3}$\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\therefore \\text { For } \\mathrm{M}_{\\mathrm{X}} \\mathrm{M}_{2} \\mathrm{Y}_4 \\\\ & \\frac{8}{3} \\times \\mathrm{x}+3 \\times 2+4(-2)=0 \\\\ & \\frac{8}{3} \\times \\mathrm{x}=2 \\\\ & \\mathrm{x}=\\frac{3}{4}=0.75\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}